<title>FRANCE: French adj Dec current a/c surplus 2.43 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French adj Dec current a/c surplus 2.43 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 2.43 billion francs in December, down from a revised 7.29 billion francs in November, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>It originally said the current account registered a 7.98 billion franc surplus in November</p>
<p>The Ministry said that the seasonally adjusted surplus in 1996 was 100.68 billion francs, compared with a 69.97 billion surplus in 1995.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed:</p>
<p>					 Dec	Nov     Oct</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)    2.43     7.29    11.58</p>
<p> Current account		  13.57     2.88    11.14</p>
<p> Goods and services	     19.51    10.75    19.51</p>
<p>  - Goods			    9.93     4.53    11.87</p>
<p>  - Services			 9.08     5.62     7.25</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.50     0.60     0.40</p>
<p> Income				0.13    -2.67    -1.76</p>
<p> Transfers			  -6.07    -5.20    -6.62</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following seasonally adjusted data on the current account in billions of francs:</p>
<p>					 Dec	Nov	Oct</p>
<p> Current account		   2.43     7.29    11.58</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 5.19     3.88     9.37</p>
<p> Services			    9.11     6.18     7.98</p>
<p>  -Travel			    4.78     4.42     6.38</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.40     0.53     0.42</p>
<p> Income			    -13.16    -0.08     2.53</p>
<p>  -Investment income	    -5.99    -0.60    -1.03</p>
<p> Transfers			  -0.49    -0.46    -0.60</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
